WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.950
Scottish actor Gerard Butler first came to
the attention of the masses as King Leonidas

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:10.680
in the 2007 epic 300, bursting onto the Hollywood
scene in a blur of muscle and blood.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.420
"This is Sparta!"

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.840
Zack Snyder's take on Frank Miller's popular
graphic novel became a huge hit, with audiences

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:26.550
digging the unique style of action and the
finely crafted physiques of Leonidas and his

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.039
Spartan warriors.

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:31.750
But was too much of the acclaim heaped on
the cast, Butler in particular?

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.380
The real test would come after 300, when the
leading man would be forced to cover up his

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.580
pecs and do some actual acting.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.110
So far, Butler seems to have had some trouble
in movies where he keeps his shirt on...and

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:44.470
here's why.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.470
Late bloomer

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.550
Butler came to acting relatively late in his
life, and at times it shows.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:54.510
The Scotsman didn't even consider becoming
an actor until the age of 27 when he saw a

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:59.130
production of Trainspotting at the Edinburgh
Festival and decided he wanted to be up on

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.580
stage himself.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:04.989
He was working at corporate law firm after
graduating from Glasgow University with a

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:09.420
law degree, though he was fired a week before
he was scheduled to be promoted from trainee

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.450
to solicitor due to his erratic behavior.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:17.200
Butler moved to London to pursue his dream
and landed a part in the production of Trainspotting

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.650
that inspired him to leave the legal profession
in the first place, returning to the Edinburgh

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.600
Festival the following year as part of the
cast.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.590
It was the start of his journey to Hollywood
stardom, though the time he spent training

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.700
to become a solicitor rather than an actor
has left him at a disadvantage.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:37.670
The skills that it takes most top actors years
of hard work to fine tune may not be present

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.530
in him, and as Butler's seemingly limited
range is further exposed with every role he

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:46.170
takes, his options become equally limited.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.460
Accent accidents

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.390
One skill that Butler hasn't been able to
develop — though not for lack of trying

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.390
— is how to mimic accents.

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:55.600
"Well, I'm actually from the states.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.080
I'm practicing my Scottish accent."

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.890
For foreigners, making it in Hollywood usually
depends on whether or not they can produce

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:08.030
something close to an American accent, yet
Butler can't seem to go more than a few sentences

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:12.200
without his broad Scottish brogue breaking
through and giving the game up.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.170
An American dialect isn't the only accent
he has had trouble with, either.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:20.310
Despite having been exposed to it throughout
his youth by Irish family members, the actor

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:25.780
personally apologized for his butchering of
the Irish accent in the 2007 romantic drama

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.780
P.S.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:28.090
I Love You.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.340
Box office blunders

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.730
The alternative to having Butler adopt an
accent is allowing him to keep his Scottish

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.840
one, though this doesn't always work out for
the best either.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.670
Gods of Egypt director Alex Proyas discovered
that first hand.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:45.940
Proyas was too busy apologizing for the whitewashing
of a film set on the African continent to

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.900
field less serious questions about Butler's
accent, though numerous critics questioned

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.920
why an Egyptian god sounded like an extra
from Braveheart.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:59.500
Accent aside, Butler's status as an A-list
leading man was on a knife's edge in the lead

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:05.090
up to 2016's Gods of Egypt, and the film's
staggering losses served as proof that he

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.900
doesn't seem to be much of a box office draw.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.580
Critical drain train

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.891
While he and the rest of the cast certainly
took it on the chin for Gods of Egypt, it

00:03:14.891 --> 00:03:18.390
wasn't the first time Butler has felt the
wrath of critics.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:22.931
The year 2016 was a particularly bad year
for the Scotsman, with pretty much all of

00:03:22.931 --> 00:03:24.900
his projects universally panned.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:30.370
Low key drama The Headhunter's Calling failed
to earn any respect, and his action sequel

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:35.760
London Has Fallen didn't fare much better,
hamstrung by allegations of casual racism

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.709
and a poor reaction to Butler as Secret Service
Agent Mike Banning.

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:44.020
Of course, none of this is anything new to
Butler, seeing as his films are rarely reviewed

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.020
positively.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:51.020
In fact, his Rotten Tomatoes filmography features
34 films — with just 5 awarded the coveted

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:57.160
Certified Fresh rating, and 23 of them scoring
50 percent or lower on the Tomatometer.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.870
CGI reliance

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:04.099
Unless you count 1997's Tomorrow Never Dies,
where Butler had a minor role in the Pierce

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:09.160
Brosnan Bond flick, only three Gerard Butler
films have managed to break that golden $100

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:12.180
million barrier in terms of lifetime gross.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.379
And those were DreamWorks' animated smash
hit How To Train Your Dragon, How to Train

00:04:16.379 --> 00:04:18.829
Your Dragon 2, and 300.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:24.410
All three of these films rely heavily on CGI
in one way or another, and the fact that Butler

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.759
has only managed to find this level of success
thanks to the work of talented animators begs

00:04:28.759 --> 00:04:33.150
the question — can Butler carry the load
when things are stripped down to the bare

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:34.540
bones?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.050
Rom-com stomp

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:41.610
It wasn't too long ago that every other phrase
searched on Google was - "Gerard Butler 300

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:46.949
workout", and that physique is still the only thing that pops in your head today when you hear his name.

00:04:46.949 --> 00:04:52.180
Zack Snyder's fantasy epic launched Butler
to stardom and set the stage for a career

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.969
as an action hero, but the actor decided to
go in the opposite direction.

00:04:55.969 --> 00:05:00.710
While he kept up the tough guy act with appearances
in Guy Ritchie's RocknRolla and crime thriller

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:06.270
Law Abiding Citizen, his most notable roles
in the years that followed 300 were in romantic

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.270
comedies.

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:08.270
P.S.

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:13.099
I Love You, The Ugly Truth, and The Bounty
Hunter were all slammed by critics and failed

00:05:13.099 --> 00:05:17.439
to transform his tough guy image into any
kind of heartthrob status.

00:05:17.439 --> 00:05:18.879
Behind-the-scenes letdowns

00:05:18.879 --> 00:05:25.360
The 2013 presidential action thriller Olympus
Has Fallen was a real labor of love for Butler,

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:29.639
a film he was passionate about and involved
with from start to finish.

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:31.309
Butler told The Independent that he

00:05:31.309 --> 00:05:35.430
"...worked so much on the script, ripping
it apart and putting it back together, really

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.629
putting flesh on the bones of it and trying
to give it some real substance and meaning

00:05:39.629 --> 00:05:44.089
in terms of a fun, action thriller that is
going be a rousing experience."

00:05:44.089 --> 00:05:49.020
He also revealed that he tries to separate
the "nasty and mean" comments from the "constructive

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:53.879
criticism" when it comes to reviews, though
he has his work cut out for him there, not

00:05:53.879 --> 00:05:58.300
only as the film's star, but as a writer and
producer, too.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.180
Unfortunately, he had to wade through a lot
of bad to get to the good because Olympus

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:05.259
Has Fallen was criticized on almost every
level.

00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:09.389
Luckily it still performed well enough at
the box office to spawn a sequel...and he'll

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:13.949
get at least one more shot to see if audiences
want to watch a third thing fall.

00:06:13.949 --> 00:06:14.949
What's next?

00:06:14.949 --> 00:06:16.370
What's next for Gerard Butler?

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.439
Well, more of the same from the look of it.

00:06:18.439 --> 00:06:23.909
The Scotsman filmed an action flick called
Hunter Killer in 2017, where he plays a submarine

00:06:23.909 --> 00:06:28.729
captain tasked with rescuing a president — though
this time it's the Russian head of state kidnapped

00:06:28.729 --> 00:06:30.009
by terrorists.

00:06:30.009 --> 00:06:34.490
And yes, Angel Has Fallen, the third film
in the Fallen franchise is still on deck for

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:40.250
release in 2018 despite the fact that the
previous two films were railed by critics.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.919
Reviewers might talk, but money walks, and
both films made enough money at the worldwide

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:48.870
box office to justify squeezing one more adventure
thriller out.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:52.909
He'll also once again provide the voice of
Stoick the Vast in How To Train Your Dragon

00:06:52.909 --> 00:06:58.469
3, slated for 2019, so we haven't heard the
last from Gerard Butler just yet...

00:06:58.469 --> 00:06:59.550
Thanks for watching!

